// Title: Access To Windows Credential History File By Uncommon Applications
// Sigma ID: 7a2a22ea-a203-4cd3-9abf-20eb1c5c6cd2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-10-17 | Modified: 2024-07-29
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1555.004
// Description: Detects file access requests to the Windows Credential History File by an uncommon application.
//   This can be a sign of credential stealing. Example case would be usage of mimikatz
//   "dpapi::credhist" function
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://tools.thehacker.recipes/mimikatz/modules/dpapi/credhist
//   - https://www.passcape.com/windows_password_recovery_dpapi_credhist
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_access/file_access_win_susp_credhist.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where FileName endswith "\\Microsoft\\Protect\\CREDHIST" and (not(((InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\system32\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\") or InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe")))
